673 - May God Be With You
 / 
Key: Eb
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 673
Topic: Sentences and Responses - 

Verse 1:
[Eb]May God be with you [Bb]Till we [Eb/Bb]meet again,
[Bb]May [Gm]God [Fm]bewith [Bb7]you, [Eb]Keep you safetill [Gm]then;
[Cm/G]And [C7/E]may [Fm]His blessings [Gm]Be [Fm/Ab]within [Eb/Bb]your heart,
[Cm]May God [Ab]bewith you [Fm/Ab]While [Eb/G]we’re [Ab]a [Cm]part,
[Bb]May God be [Eb]withyou.

Verse 2:
[Eb]May God be with you, [Bb]Watch you [Eb/Bb]from above,
[Bb]May [Gm]God [Fm]protect [Eb]you [Ab/Eb]in [Eb]His tender [Gm]love;
[Cm/G]And [C7/E]with [Fm]the dawning [Gm]Of [Fm/Ab]each [Eb/Bb]bright, new day,
[Cm]May God [Ab]be with you, [Fm/Ab]To [Ab]guide [Eb/G]your [Ab]way,
[Bb]May God be [Eb]with you.
